      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, there are several factors that could lead to yellow or brown patches in your grass, aside from nutrient deficiencies. Pests such as grubs or chinch bugs can cause rust-colored feeding damage, resulting in those patchy areas. Soil compaction is another possible culprit, which can affect water and nutrient uptake by the grass roots. Additionally, poor soil drainage, drought stress, or disease can also lead to similar visual symptoms. It's wise to inspect for visible signs of pests, look for changes in soil structure or crusting, and check for any patterns in watering or drainage issues in your yard to get a better understanding of what might be causing your lawn to struggle. If unsure, consider consulting with a local turf specialist for a more in-depth diagnosis.",
